WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.313
OT threats include cybercriminals, ransomware operators, insiders, contractors, state-linked groups, hacktivists, and accidental users.

00:00:07.313 --> 00:00:18.871
Their goals and capabilities differ, but several actors may exploit the same weak account, remote pathway, exposed service, or poorly controlled engineering workstation.

00:00:18.871 --> 00:00:29.487
Common vulnerabilities include unsupported operating systems, unpatched devices, insecure protocols, weak or shared authentication, excessive privileges, flat networks, and limited monitoring.

00:00:29.487 --> 00:00:42.461
Remote access may be necessary for maintenance, yet permanently enabled tunnels and unmanaged vendor endpoints create risk if identity, approval, and session activity are not controlled.

00:00:42.461 --> 00:00:46.943
Misconfiguration and poor change control are also vulnerabilities.

00:00:46.943 --> 00:00:53.784
An incorrect firewall rule can expose a control zone or interrupt required traffic.

00:00:53.784 --> 00:00:58.266
An undocumented logic change can affect process behavior.

00:00:58.266 --> 00:01:02.748
A temporary connection may remain long after maintenance.

00:01:02.748 --> 00:01:07.701
These conditions can cause incidents without a sophisticated attacker.

00:01:07.701 --> 00:01:12.183
Technical severity alone does not establish OT risk.

00:01:12.183 --> 00:01:27.516
Analysts must confirm that the affected feature is present, determine whether the asset is reachable, understand what it controls, identify independent safeguards, and evaluate the consequences of both exploitation and remediation.

00:01:27.516 --> 00:01:34.357
Patching a vulnerable system may still require testing and an approved maintenance window.

00:01:34.357 --> 00:01:39.311
Threat and vulnerability analysis should therefore produce operational decisions.

00:01:39.311 --> 00:01:48.511
Reduce unnecessary access, monitor important boundaries, protect privileged tools, apply compensating controls, schedule remediation, and document residual risk.

00:01:48.511 --> 00:01:52.993
The goal is not a larger finding count.

00:01:52.993 --> 00:02:01.249
It is a defensible understanding of which weaknesses can produce meaningful harm in the actual process.
